  "content": {
    "text": "Market Extra\nAngst over SpaceX IPO adds to dive in tech stocks\nTech stocks fall sharply Tuesday, but investors aren’t bailing on the rest of the S&P 500\nTechnology stocks tumbled on Tuesday, extending a swoon that began in early June, as investors anxiously await the historic SpaceX IPO later this week and retreat from hot parts of the artificial-intelligence playbook.\nThe concern is two-fold: For one, SpaceX SPCX is currently planning to supply the public with up to $86 billion worth of its shares; and two, there’s the worry that investors will have to raise cash to buy up that supply by trimming stakes in their recent winners.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "Market Extra",
      "Angst over SpaceX IPO adds to dive in tech stocks",
      "Tech stocks fall sharply Tuesday, but investors aren’t bailing on the rest of the S&P 500",
      "Technology stocks tumbled on Tuesday, extending a swoon that began in early June, as investors anxiously await the historic SpaceX IPO later this week and retreat from hot parts of the artificial-intelligence playbook.",
      "The concern is two-fold: For one, SpaceX SPCX is currently planning to supply the public with up to $86 billion worth of its shares; and two, there’s the worry that investors will have to raise cash to buy up that supply by trimming stakes in their recent winners."
